<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Integration manifest for Machine1 == the four Adaptive Applications.

  Everything machine-specific lives here: which process runs where, which
  function-group state starts it, which SOME/IP instance backs each port, and
  which IAM grants make the calls legal at run time.

  FUNCTION GROUP MAPPING == the part worth reading

              Off   Driving   Degraded   Safe
    sensingd   ==      X         X
    perceptiond ==     X         X
    planningd  ==      X
    controld   ==      X         X         X

  On SetState(AvPilotFG.Degraded), EM stops planningd and leaves the other
  three running. No C++ implements that; the table above is the whole
  mechanism, and it is the one capability this port buys that ROS 2 cannot
  express.

  What Degraded means behaviourally: Control keeps the last trajectory and
  follows the remainder of its 20-step steering horizon with decay, then
  commands a safe stop when its staleness gate fires. Sensing and Perception
  keep running so the logs and the overlay still show why. Safe stops
  everything except Control, which holds the vehicle stationary.

  STARTUP ORDERING is deliberately NOT expressed as an EM ExecutionDependency
  of perceptiond on sensingd. The FrameDescriptor protocol already handles a
  late or restarted producer == segmentInstanceId changes, the consumer
  re-maps, valid gates the read == and that covers cases EM ordering does not,
  such as sensingd being restarted while perceptiond keeps running. If you do
  want the EM-level ordering as well, it belongs in perceptiond's
  STATE-DEPENDENT-STARTUP-CONFIG below.

  SCHEDULING: all four ask for SCHED_RR. EM downgrades this to SCHED_OTHER
  with a warning when it lacks CAP_SYS_NICE, and starts the process anyway ==
  the silent downgrade is the dangerous part, so check the boot log rather
  than assuming the priorities below are in force.
-->
<AUTOSAR xmlns="http://autosar.org/schema/r4.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://autosar.org/schema/r4.0 AUTOSAR_00049.xsd">
  <AR-PACKAGES>
    <AR-PACKAGE>
      <SHORT-NAME>AvDeployment</SHORT-NAME>
      <ELEMENTS>

